invariant: INV-6
file: handshake_parser.c
catches: handshake_strict_webpki
reason: the TRUST=webpki CertificateVerify parser admits rsa_pkcs1_sha256,
  which the ClientHello offers for certificate signatures only, so a
  server could sign the handshake with PKCS#1 v1.5, which RFC 9846
  §4.4.3 forbids there. bin/handshake_strict_webpki's refused rows object.

--- old
    return algorithm == SIGALG_RSA_PSS_RSAE_SHA256 || algorithm == SIGALG_ECDSA_P256_SHA256 ||
           algorithm == SIGALG_ECDSA_P384_SHA384;
--- new
    return algorithm == SIGALG_RSA_PSS_RSAE_SHA256 || algorithm == SIGALG_ECDSA_P256_SHA256 ||
           algorithm == SIGALG_ECDSA_P384_SHA384 || algorithm == SIGALG_RSA_PKCS1_SHA256;
